I was somewhat disappointed in my last game at the Astral plane...
Not realizing in time that I was conflicting with my Sceptre of Might
I entered a temple and observed the High Priest and some other human
inhabitant fight each other. I was already in some trouble, I thought,
since in an attempt to polymorph my pet zombie (formerly a purple worm)
into something more useful my pet shuddered and disintegrated, and all
I was left with was a rolling thunder from above. So I kept conflicting
because I did not want my artifact to ignore me next time if I switch
it off now, and I was quite sure that I will have to visit one or both
of the other altars (as usual). But then the High Priest died in his
fight, the other one was killed with a single strike by me, and I saw
that it was _my_ own altar and the High Priest of my own god. I did not
expect that my god would make *me* to the legal successor of the High
Priest, rather I thought I may be in some trouble when trying to offer
the Amulet. But nothing special happened. I was neither punished for my
misbehaviour nor promoted to be the new High Priest. Well, what could
a cavewoman expect...

